isBoolean -- Determine if a poset is a boolean algebra.
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        r = isBoolean(P)
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: (Posets)Poset,, The poset to be
        tested
  * Outputs:
      * r, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, Whether the given
        poset is a boolean algebra or not

Description
===========

Every finite boolean algebra is atomic and the number of atoms determines its
isomorphism class.

This makes it possible to use the *note atoms: (Posets)atoms, method to
determine the necessary isomorphism class of P and use the *note areIsomorphic:
(Posets)areIsomorphic, method to check if the required isomorphism holds.



+---------------------------+
|i1 : P = booleanLattice(3);|
+---------------------------+
|i2 : isBoolean(P)          |
|                           |
|o2 = true                  |
+---------------------------+

Ways to use isBoolean:
======================

  * "isBoolean(Poset)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note isBoolean: isBoolean, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

